# Orchestrator & roadmap

Dispatch One is built **task-by-task** from `docs/dispatch-one-development-roadmap.md`. Sub-agents implement tasks; a verifier checks them; checkboxes get ticked.

## Use the orchestrator skill when

- The user asks to "orchestrate", "delegate", "run the roadmap", "implement phase X", or "execute tasks autonomously"
- Multi-step work spans several tasks

In that case, follow `.cursor/skills/orchestrator/SKILL.md`. Do not improvise.

## Use the roadmap directly when

- You're implementing a single task and the user already pointed at a Task ID (e.g. `P2-01`)
- You're checking dependencies or what's next

Open `docs/dispatch-one-development-roadmap.md`, search the Task ID, read the row (Doc Ref + acceptance criteria + Tests).

## Task lifecycle (plan-file mode)

```
- [ ] not started
- [~] awaiting verification    ← Lane S: execution agent (if plan file in WRITE SCOPE)
                               ← Lane P: orchestrator at batch start
- [x] verified                 ← Lane S: task verifier on staging
                               ← Lane P: staging batch verifier after integration
- [!] failed — <reason>        ← verifier only
```

If you're acting as the orchestrator chat: never edit checkboxes yourself during normal flow except **Lane P batch prep** (`[~]` at batch start). Verifiers update `[x]` / `[!]`.

**Parallel batches (Lane P):** execution on isolated worktrees (`best-of-n-runner`); integration merges to `staging`. See orchestrator SKILL.md § Parallelism.

## Jira board status (when orchestrating)

Project **DO** on `mdg-labs.atlassian.net`. Commit suffixes use Jira keys: `(DO-47)`.

- **Execution agents** → set **In Progress** on leaf issue(s) and epic parent when dispatching a child (first action, before code); set **In Review** before verifier handoff
- **Verification agents** → set **Done** only after all layers PASS; FAIL → **Ready** + comment
- Execution prompts must **not** include Done transition IDs — see orchestrator SKILL.md and `jira-board.md`

## Universal acceptance criteria (every task)

Even when not listed in a task row, the verifier applies §1.6 of the roadmap:

- File / directory naming (rule `04-naming.mdc`)
- Conventional commits (rule `01-git-workflow.mdc`)
- TypeScript strict, no `any`, no `console.log` (rule `typescript.mdc`)
- Security defaults — no logged secrets, server-side validation, Prisma-only DB
- i18n — every UI string via `next-intl`

## Non-goals (do not implement)

See **§6 Explicit non-goals** in the roadmap. Examples that are out of MVP scope: map-based dispatching, alliance treasury spending, gameplay events, auto-suggest loadout, hospital bed capacity, PWA, email verification, password reset, account self-deletion.

If a request lands inside a non-goal, **flag it** and ask whether to defer.
